# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b1), edited. alda_farnum's first conversation.

~ start
set alda_farnum_met
Narrator: The hearth smells of spiced cider, and the woman behind the bar smells of lavender water and brass coin.
alda_farnum [smile]: Mind the mud on the runner, my dears. You look like guests who can afford a hot bath and a bed.
* Ask about rooms and the inn -> about_work
* Ask about Wickermoor Village -> about_village
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask what folk are talking about lately -> rumour
* [Perception DC 14] Study her jewelry and the books behind the bar -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ about_work
alda_farnum [smile]: Single room is one gold piece, a triple is two, with a hot bath and Twilight breakfast. We have a stage for players and four beasts in the stable.
-> menu

~ about_village
alda_farnum [neutral]: Keep on the right side of Mayor Somerton's paperwork, pay your tab before dawnless morning, and the Green Queen will smile on you, darlings.
-> menu

~ shop_open
alda_farnum [smile]: Let us see what comforts your purse is ready for tonight.
services
-> menu

~ rumour
alda_farnum [sly]: Half the parish is coughing up marsh-damp, and two south lane lads never came home from the heather. Bad for tempers, wonderful for hot toddy sales.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
set cult_clue_alda_farnum
Narrator: Silver hares with tiny antlers swing from her ears, and a sap-stained leather book sits beside her ledger.
alda_farnum [sly]: Staring does not buy a drink, sweetheart. An innkeeper must track every debt in this hollow, old ones included.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
Narrator: She clicks her brass abacus shut before you can read a single name on her open page.
alda_farnum [smile]: Looking for a discount written in the margins, love? My prices are quite fixed.
-> menu

